<3 Working Problem 3: Collatz Steps

<3 Read starting number
n :=) -0-0-

steps :=) 0.0
max_val :=) n
one :=) 1.0
two :=) 2.0
three_const :=) 3.0
zero :=) 0.0

<3 Main Collatz loop
D:< (n :!=) one) ><(((,^>
  <3 Update max value if current n is larger
  :) (n :>) max_val)
    max_val :=) n
  
  <3 Collatz step: if even divide by 2, if odd multiply by 3 and add 1
  remainder :=) n :%) two
  :) (remainder :==) zero)
    n :=) n :/) two
  :(
    temp :=) three_const :*) n
    n :=) temp :+) one
  
  <3 Increment step counter
  steps :=) steps :+) one
<^,)))><

<3 Print results matching Python format
:P("steps =")
:P(steps)
:P("max =")
:P(max_val)